.TH BRKAS\-CONTAINER 1 "2026-11-13" "brkas" "User Commands"
.SH NAME
brkas\-container \- run brkas in a container
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B brkas\-container
[\fIoptions\fR] \fIbrkas-command\fR [\fIarguments\fR]
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B brkas\-container
runs a
.BR brkas (1)
command in a Docker or Podman container, as the calling user.
.PP
The image is a Debian with the host packages of Buildroot, cmake and brkas.
When the default image is missing, it is built from the Dockerfile shipped
with brkas.
.PP
Shared with the container, at the same paths: the work directory, the
directories of the project files, the download cache, the output root and the
current directory. The home directory has the same path and starts empty.
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
.BI \-\-engine " engine"
\fBpodman\fR or \fBdocker\fR. Default: \fBcontainer.engine\fR of the
project, else the one installed, podman first.
.TP
.BI \-\-image " image"
Default: \fB$BRKAS_CONTAINER_IMAGE\fR, else \fBcontainer.image\fR of the
project, else \fBbrkas:\fR\fIversion\fR.
.TP
.B \-\-build\-image
Build the image from the Dockerfile shipped with brkas.
.TP
.BI \-\-work\-dir " dir"
Work directory. Default: \fB$BRKAS_WORK_DIR\fR, else the current directory.
.TP
.BI \-\-mount " dir"
Share \fIdir\fR read-write, at the same path. May be repeated.
.TP
.B \-\-ssh\-agent
Forward the SSH agent of \fB$SSH_AUTH_SOCK\fR.
.TP
.BI \-\-ssh\-dir " dir"
Mount \fIdir\fR read-only and copy it to \fB~/.ssh\fR in the container.
Default: \fB$BRKAS_SSH_DIR\fR. The container can read every key in it.
.TP
.BI \-\-engine\-option " option"
Pass \fIoption\fR to \fIengine\fR \fBrun\fR. May be repeated.
.PP
\fBcontainer.options\fR of the project are passed the same way. The
\fBxconfig\fR command is not available.
.SH ENVIRONMENT
.TP
.B BRKAS_CONTAINER_IMAGE
Default image.
.TP
.B BRKAS_WORK_DIR
Default work directory.
.TP
.B BRKAS_SSH_DIR
Default of \fB\-\-ssh\-dir\fR.
.TP
.BR http_proxy ", " https_proxy ", " no_proxy ", " TERM
Passed to the container, also in upper case for the proxies.
.SH EXIT STATUS
The status of the brkas command, or of the image build.
.SH EXAMPLE
.nf
brkas\-container \-\-mount ~/src/myapp shell demo.yml
.fi
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR brkas (1)
